      "claim": "Krubera (Voronya, 'Crows' Cave') is in the Arabika Massif, Abkhazia, with its entrance at 2,256 m and a ~60 m entrance shaft where crows nest; a 2024 resurvey gave a depth of 2,224 m, ending in a flooded sump",
